.el .ds Aq '
.TH xil-sfx-restore 1  "xil-sfx-restore " 
.SH NAME
xil\-sfx\-restore \- Reapply journaled timeline sound edits (sfx_<tag>_edits.jsonl) onto the episode\*(Aqs SFX config — recovery for a cleared or regenerated sfx_<tag>.json.
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBxil\-sfx\-restore\fR [\fB\-\-episode\fR] [\fB\-\-tag\fR] [\fB\-\-show\fR] [\fB\-\-sfx\fR] [\fB\-\-dry\-run\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] 
.SH DESCRIPTION
Reapply journaled timeline sound edits (sfx_<tag>_edits.jsonl) onto the episode\*(Aqs SFX config — recovery for a cleared or regenerated sfx_<tag>.json.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-episode\fR \fI<EPISODE>\fR
Episode tag (e.g. S04E04)
.TP
\fB\-\-tag\fR \fI<TAG>\fR
Raw non\-episodic tag (e.g. V01C03)
.TP
\fB\-\-show\fR \fI<SHOW>\fR
Show name override (default: from project.json)
.TP
\fB\-\-sfx\fR \fI<SFX>\fR
Override SFX config path
.TP
\fB\-\-dry\-run\fR
Report what would be reapplied without writing
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
